                <head>Chapter VI: October 12–November 22, 1937</head>
                <p>Problem of Ending Far Eastern Conflict; effect on Far East of Berlin–Rome–Tokyo
                        <hi rendition="#italic">rapprochement</hi>, October 15; French ban on
                    transit of war material through Indochina, October 19; President Roosevelt’s
                    reaction thereto, October 22; modification of French transit ban, October 23,
                    November 10; preparations for transfer of Chinese Government westward from
                    Nanking, November 16; Ambassador Grew’s review of efforts on behalf of peaceful
                    settlement of Far Eastern conflict, November 18; Chinese Government’s
                    announcement of removal from Nanking to Chungking, November 20; Generalissimo
                    Chiang’s message to President Roosevelt, November 22</p>







































































































































